# PM Surya Ghar Yojana – App Feature Overview (`solar_app_v4`)

> A full breakdown of every feature in the application, organized by page and backend layer.

---

## 🏠 1. Home Page (`/` → [index.html](file:///d:/All%20projects/PM%20Surya%20Ghar%20Yojana/1.%20prototypes/solar_app_v4/templates/index.html))

### Hero Section
- **Full-screen background image** that changes between a day image (light mode) and a night/solar image (dark mode) with a smooth fade-out/fade-in transition.
- **Centered overlay box** (glassmorphism effect with backdrop blur) containing the headline *"Powering India's Solar Revolution"*.
- A **"View Features"** button that smoothly scrolls the user down to the content sections.

### Dark / Light Mode Toggle
- A **fixed floating button** (top-right corner, moon/sun icon) lets users toggle between dark and light modes.
- The chosen preference is **saved to `localStorage`** and persists across page visits and page refreshes.
- Both the background photo and all UI colours adapt instantly.
- In dark mode, the main headings get a **cyan animated glowing gradient** effect; in light mode they are a solid navy blue.

### About PM Surya Ghar Yojana Section
Describes the national scheme with four bold bullet points:
- Mission: free electricity for 1 crore households.
- ₹75,000 crore government investment.
- Need for a reliable verification system.
- Challenge of scaling traditional field inspections.

### Benefits Carousel (right of the About section)
An **auto-rotating carousel** with dot-navigation showing 6 benefit cards:
1. For Residential Users – subsidies up to ₹78,000
2. For Commercial Users – accelerated depreciation & tax benefits
3. Free Electricity – reduce bills significantly
4. Income Opportunity – sell excess power back to the grid
5. Substantial Subsidies – up to 60% on installation costs
6. Green Energy – contribute to India's renewable goals

Each card uses a **glassmorphism glow-box** style with an appropriate icon and a hover lift animation.

### AI-Powered Solar Analysis CTA
A highlighted box with animated amber gradient background, describing the AI verification system. A **"Start AI Analysis"** button with a rocket icon and a launch animation (shimmer + thrust effect) redirects to `/ai-analysis`.

### Quick Actions Section
Two action boxes side-by-side:
- **Subsidy Calculator** – links to the `/subsidy` page.
- **Application Flowchart** – links to the `/process` page.

Both cards have a hover lift effect and are styled with a green/blue glassmorphism background respectively.

---

## 🤖 2. AI-Powered Solar Analysis Page (`/ai-analysis` → [AIPSI.html](file:///d:/All%20projects/PM%20Surya%20Ghar%20Yojana/1.%20prototypes/solar_app_v4/templates/AIPSI.html))

This is the core feature page of the app. It uses **ArcGIS JS API 4.30** for mapping and the **Roboflow cloud ML model** for solar panel detection.

### Input Data Panel
- **Sample ID** – auto-generated (read-only).
- **Latitude / Longitude** manual input fields.
- **Search Buffer** – fixed at 1200 sq.ft radius (read-only).
- **CSV Upload (optional)** – upload a `.csv` file with [sample_id](file:///d:/All%20projects/PM%20Surya%20Ghar%20Yojana/1.%20prototypes/solar_app_v4/app.py#160-162), `latitude`, `longitude` columns for batch processing.
- **"Use Selected Location"** button – transfers coordinates from the map to the input fields.
- **"Analyze Location"** button – triggers the backend API call to fetch satellite imagery and run Roboflow inference.

### Interactive Map (Select Location Panel)
- Full **ArcGIS/Esri World Imagery** map embedded directly in the page.
- A **search bar** with live autocomplete suggestions (geocoding) overlaid on the map.
- Click anywhere on the map to place a marker and **automatically populate the lat/lon fields**.
- Below the map: **Selected Latitude**, **Selected Longitude**, and **Address** display fields that update in real time.

### Analysis Results Panel (shown after analysis)
Appears once the user clicks "Analyze Location". Shows:
- **Solar Panels Detected** (Yes/No with colour coding: green = verified, red = not verified)
- **Estimated Panel Count**
- **Confidence Score** (0.000–1.000)
- **Estimated PV Area**
- **Estimated Capacity** (kW)
- **QC Status** (VERIFIED / PARTIAL / PENDING)

### 3D Satellite View Panel (shown after analysis)
- An **ArcGIS 3D SceneView** renders the selected location with photorealistic World Imagery tiles.
- Displays **real 3D building models** (where available).
- Live **Altitude** and **Tilt** readouts in the corner.
- Three scene control buttons:
  - 🧭 **Compass / Reset North**
  - 🏠 **Reset View** (zoom back to the location)
  - ↩ **Reset Tilt**
- Metadata fields below: Imagery Source (*World Imagery*), Resolution (*30 cm*), 3D Buildings (*Enabled*).

### Detailed Results Section
Shown when the user clicks **"View Detailed Results / Download Results"**:

#### Analysis Summary (3-column grid)
| Column 1 | Column 2 | Column 3 |
|---|---|---|
| Solar Panels Detected | Confidence Score | Estimated Capacity |
| Estimated Panel Count | Estimated PV Area | QC Status |

#### Quality Control Notes
- Bullet list of QC checks returned by the model.
- A summary paragraph about the scan quality.

#### JSON Output
- A dark-themed `<pre>` block showing the **raw JSON** returned by the Roboflow API.
- A **"Download JSON"** button to save the result as a `.json` file.

#### Action Buttons
- **"New Analysis"** – resets the UI to start fresh.
- **"Save to Database"** – posts the result to the `/api/save-analysis` backend endpoint.

---

## 💰 3. Subsidy Calculator (`/subsidy` → [Subsidy.html](file:///d:/All%20projects/PM%20Surya%20Ghar%20Yojana/1.%20prototypes/solar_app_v4/templates/Subsidy.html))

### Interactive Slider Calculator
- **System Capacity slider** – range 1 kW to 10 kW (default 3 kW).
- **State dropdown** – Delhi, Maharashtra, Karnataka, Tamil Nadu, Gujarat.
- Subsidy is **recalculated live** as the slider or state selection changes.
- Formula used:
  - ≤ 3 kW → ₹14,588 per kW
  - > 3 kW → ₹14,588 × 3 + ₹7,294 × (capacity − 3)
  - Multiplied by a state-level factor (e.g., 0.90 for Karnataka).
- **Estimated Subsidy Range** displayed in a prominent blue banner (e.g., *₹32,000 – ₹36,000*).

### Subsidy Information Section
Two-column layout:

**Eligibility Criteria**
- Residential consumers only
- Valid electricity connection required
- Suitable rooftop required
- System capacity within a defined range

**Subsidy Rate Table**
| Capacity | Rate |
|---|---|
| Up to 3 kW | ₹14,588 per kW |
| Above 3 kW | ₹7,294 per kW |
| Maximum | 10 kW |

> Note: These figures are labelled *"to be approved yet"* in the UI.

### Floating Home Button
A pulsing blue circular button (bottom-right) that navigates back to the home page.

---

## 📋 4. Application Process / How It Works (`/process` → [process.html](file:///d:/All%20projects/PM%20Surya%20Ghar%20Yojana/1.%20prototypes/solar_app_v4/templates/process.html))

A **6-step vertical flowchart** with animated step connectors (lines + arrows between each step).

| Step | Icon | Title | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| 01 | 📍 | Select Location on Map | Choose location via map click or search. Coordinates auto-filled with address display. |
| 02 | 🎯 | Use Selected Coordinates | Transfer lat/long to input fields. Sample ID generated automatically from coordinates. |
| 03 | 🔍 | Initiate AI Analysis | Start analysis with 1200 sq.ft radius scan. AI processes satellite imagery automatically. |
| 04 | 🛰️ | View 3D Satellite Results | Interactive 3D view with controls. Altitude, tilt, and imagery details displayed. |
| 05 | 📊 | Review Analysis Summary | Panel detection, count, area, capacity results. Confidence score and QC status shown. |
| 06 | 💾 | Download / Save Results | Download JSON report or save to database. Start new analysis or view details. |

Each step card has:
- A numbered badge in the top-left corner.
- A blue left-border accent.
- A hover lift animation.
- A connecting line + arrow pointing to the next step.

A **"Start Analysis Now"** button at the bottom redirects to [AIPSI.html](file:///d:/All%20projects/PM%20Surya%20Ghar%20Yojana/1.%20prototypes/solar_app_v4/templates/AIPSI.html).

---

## 📬 5. Contact Page (`/contact` → [contact.html](file:///d:/All%20projects/PM%20Surya%20Ghar%20Yojana/1.%20prototypes/solar_app_v4/templates/contact.html))

### Contact Form
Fields: First Name, Last Name, Email Address, Contact Number, Message (non-resizable textarea). Submitted to **Formspree** (`POST https://formspree.io/f/xwpgqryb`) via [fetch()](file:///d:/All%20projects/PM%20Surya%20Ghar%20Yojana/1.%20prototypes/solar_app_v4/templates/AIPSI.html#1383-1420).
- Shows a **loading spinner** while submitting.
- Shows a **green success** or **red error** message after submission.
- On success (after 1.5 s), the contact info box on the right column **slides out** and is replaced by the Live Chat.

### Contact Information Box (right column, initial state)
- Office address, helpline, email, and working hours (all marked *"to be updated yet"*).
- A **"Chat with us (live)"** button that launches the Ably live chat directly.

### Live Chat (Ably Realtime)
- Powered by the **Ably Realtime SDK**.
- Channel: `solar-expert-chat`.
- Features:
  - Random username auto-assigned and saved in `localStorage` (e.g., `User472`).
  - **Message history** – loads the last 20 messages on join.
  - **Real-time message delivery** – all connected users see new messages instantly.
  - Messages are styled differently for **sent** (right-aligned, dark blue), **received** (left-aligned, dark grey), and **system** (centred, italic) messages.
  - System messages indicate connection status (connected / failed).

---

## 🔧 6. Backend – Flask API ([app.py](file:///d:/All%20projects/PM%20Surya%20Ghar%20Yojana/1.%20prototypes/solar_app_v4/app.py))

The app runs on **Flask** (Python), serving both HTML templates and a REST API.

### Template Routes

| Route | Template |
|---|---|
| `GET /` | [index.html](file:///d:/All%20projects/PM%20Surya%20Ghar%20Yojana/1.%20prototypes/solar_app_v4/templates/index.html) |
| `GET /ai-analysis` | [AIPSI.html](file:///d:/All%20projects/PM%20Surya%20Ghar%20Yojana/1.%20prototypes/solar_app_v4/templates/AIPSI.html) |
| `GET /subsidy` | [Subsidy.html](file:///d:/All%20projects/PM%20Surya%20Ghar%20Yojana/1.%20prototypes/solar_app_v4/templates/Subsidy.html) |
| `GET /process` | [process.html](file:///d:/All%20projects/PM%20Surya%20Ghar%20Yojana/1.%20prototypes/solar_app_v4/templates/process.html) |
| `GET /contact` | [contact.html](file:///d:/All%20projects/PM%20Surya%20Ghar%20Yojana/1.%20prototypes/solar_app_v4/templates/contact.html) |

### API Endpoints

#### ML / Detection
| Method & Route | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `POST /api/analyze-image` | Upload an image file → run Roboflow inference → return detection results (panel count, confidence, bounding boxes) |
| `POST /api/analyze-location` | Send lat/lon → fetch Esri satellite tile → run Roboflow inference → return detection results |
| `POST /api/annotate-image` | Upload an image → run local model → return annotated image with bounding boxes |

#### Subsidy
| Method & Route | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `POST /api/subsidy` | Given a [sample_id](file:///d:/All%20projects/PM%20Surya%20Ghar%20Yojana/1.%20prototypes/solar_app_v4/app.py#160-162) (from a previous analysis), calculate and return a subsidy range in INR |

#### Data / Results
| Method & Route | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `POST /api/upload-csv` | Upload a CSV of image paths → batch-run inference → return results |
| `POST /api/save-analysis` | Save analysis JSON result to disk and in-memory store |
| `GET /api/download-results/<id>` | Download the JSON result for a given sample ID |
| `GET /samples` | List all analysis results in the current session |
| `GET /sample/<sample_id>` | Retrieve a specific analysis result |
| `GET /api/health` | Health check – returns model connectivity status and session statistics |

---

## 🤖 7. ML / Roboflow Integration

### Cloud Inference (Primary)
- Uses the **Roboflow REST API** (`https://api.roboflow.com/infer/<model_id>`).
- Model: `custom-workflow-object-detection-tgnqc-af4gr/1` (custom-trained solar panel detector).
- Workflow:
  1. Download satellite image from the Esri tile URL.
  2. Base64-encode the image.
  3. POST to Roboflow API with the encoded image and API key.
  4. Parse predictions (class, confidence, bounding box x/y/width/height).

### Optional Local Inference (Fallback)
- A **RetinaNet** (ResNet-50 FPN backbone) local model path is configured.
- PyTorch, PIL/NumPy, and pycocotools are imported with **graceful fallback** if not installed.
- Local model is not loaded by default — the cloud model takes priority.

### SolarAnalysisSystem Class
An in-memory result store that:
- Generates unique `SOLAR_XXXX` sample IDs.
- Caches all analysis results by sample ID for later retrieval.
- Provides a subsidy calculation method (capacity × state multiplier).

---

## 🎨 8. UI Design System

### Color Modes
Full **light/dark theming** via CSS custom properties. Both modes define:
`--bg-primary`, `--bg-secondary`, `--text-primary`, `--text-secondary`, `--border-color`, `--header-bg`, `--accent-color`, `--input-bg`, `--input-text`, `--input-border`.

### Typography
`'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif` throughout all pages.

### Key Animations
| Animation | Where Used |
|---|---|
| `float` (translateY up/down) | Solar panel icons in the header |
| `colorShift` + `glowPulse` | Page headings in dark mode (cyan gradient) |
| `pulsatingBorder` | Highlighted elements, animated borders |
| `pulse` / `pulse-glow` | Floating home button |
| `thrust` / `blurLine` | Rocket button on the home page |
| Benefit carousel fade | Homepage benefits carousel |

### Component Styles
- **`glow-box`** – glassmorphism cards with blue gradient background.
- **`quick-action-box`** – green glassmorphism cards.
- **`ai-analysis-box`** – amber glassmorphism box.
- **`analysis-card`** – clean card with border and hover lift.
- **`primary-button`** / **`blue-button`** – consistent button styles across all pages.

